> CleanupSpec_6_v2 -- DRAFT (footprint-check, 2026-11-10; NOT approved, not used by any config).
> Copy of STAGE1_alloy/models/CleanupSpec_6.als (Saileshwar and Qureshi, MICRO 2019). Only the protection-set clause in the
> "Specific defense model" block changes, plus this header; everything else is byte-identical
> to CleanupSpec_6.als (and therefore to STT_6.als outside the defense block).
>   - protection set = all memory AND every register the test never writes (its initial value),
>     never untainted. Values computed from either are protected through rf/ddi as before.
>     CleanupSpec_6 protects memory only, so a speculative load whose address comes from an initial
>     register, or from ALU work on initial registers, with no load in the chain (AMuLeT's UV6
>     shape) cannot be generated there.
>   - speculation contract (after an unresolved branch) and leakage (load addresses) unchanged.
> See wiki/design/MODELS_AND_BUILDS.md PART 8, '2026-11-10 -- Paper check of the footprint models'.
